 "text": "1. B: \"loves\" takes the direct object \"me\", so it is a transitive verb.\n2. A: Alamgir Kabir directed \"Dhire Bohe Meghna\".\n3. A: Something that has undergone \"লয়\" is called \"লীন\".\n4. B: The cupula helps maintain balance. Options B and C are very close; I chose B as the more common textbook wording, but this is uncertain.\n5. D: The 2012 Olympics were held in London.\n6. D: Sarcopterygians have a diphycercal tail.\n7. D: The main parts of a spectrometer are the collimator, telescope and prism table, so a lens is not one of them.\n8. A: Mahasthangarh is on the bank of the Karatoya.\n9. C: ASCII actually stands for \"American Standard Code for Information Interchange\". None of the options is exactly right, and C is the closest.\n10. A: Silicon (14 electrons) is 1s² 2s² 2p⁶ 3s² 3p².\n11. A: I am not confident here, since sources give different counts; 34 is my best guess.\n12. B: The noun form of \"compel\" is \"compulsion\".\n13. B: The smaller part is 2/5 of 20 ft, which is 8 ft.\n14. C: Halley's Comet appears about every 76 years.\n15. C: If the areas are in ratio 3 : 1, the sides are in ratio √3 : 1, and so are the perimeters.\n\n{\"answers\": {\"1f33fe18-fe2f-4931-8755-5c125d73f6f3-141588\": \"B\", \"1f420286-ce01-4588-9531-08e9a30f3e00-9720\": \"A\", \"1fc36e4b-f174-4e9b-affe-72c5b554c69e-112068\": \"A\", \"1fe94d60-0be9-4d28-95c2-6c61a9527b81-43494\": \"B\", \"20237bbf-9ee7-4adb-86a4-8f00bc58395d-50654\": \"D\", \"20878697-22ad-4a7e-aa1b-186712c7546a-11230\": \"D\", \"20cdd0e6-5505-4341-ab58-be8a0798ef9b-129961\": \"D\", \"22b6200c-967e-4c1e-b795-83428fd19ea9-38564\": \"A\", \"2412d1aa-700c-48b9-9eb9-16471aa49b94-35928\": \"C\", \"2482426f-80eb-49f5-85ae-f006e676c3d9-88630\": \"A\", \"2585bc61-6f4f-41d4-bfb2-2c1f7753142f-100344\": \"A\", \"25deb312-85ad-41bd-937b-ba75f1903f5a-90417\": \"B\", \"25fb65ff-56a2-498a-b741-889ff05095a5-64096\": \"B\", \"27ab6b9b-c362-4f64-98b5-11fa18c16f03-52700\": \"C\", \"27dad806-6307-41a0-9f25-89f836a25269-1